{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "John Meets Sandra"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Peter's News"}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 7}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le07ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The First Conditional "}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use the first conditional to say it's possible that you will do something. In that condition, something else will happen."}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can start the sentence with <span class=\"italic\">when</span>, <span class=\"italic\">after</span> and <span class=\"italic\">once</span> to say what the result will be when we do something or after we finish an action."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> clause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Main Clause \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" If you cook the meat too long, \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"it will burn. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's possible you will cook the meat too long. In this condition: it will burn.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If I ask the teacher to help me,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I will pass the test.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's possible I will ask the teacher to help me. In this condition: I will pass the test.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If he gets a high-paying job,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"he can go on a vacation twice a year.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's possible he will get a high-paying job. In this condition: he can go on vacation twice a year.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "After I pass my test, I will look for a better job."}, {"type": "example", "content": " When I get a high-paying job, I might need to buy new work clothes. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Once I start making a lot of money, I will go on a cruise."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "anxious"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " being afraid or nervous about what may happen"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: I'm anxious about my test coming up."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le07ob02aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are some words you use to talk about your job or career."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "relieved "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "feeling relaxed and happy because something difficult passed/finished "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm so relieved my test is done."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le07ob02aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Guess what? "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "You say this before you tell someone something interesting or surprising to catch their attention."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: Guess what? I just got a new job. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le07ob02aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "investment firm "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a company that uses your money to buy stock in another company to make more money "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Peter's business skills helped him get a job in an investment firm."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le07ob02aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "I'll take it. "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "You say this when we decide to purchase an item or accept an offer. "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: The company offered me the job. I think I'll take it."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le07ob02aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "career "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a job for a number of years in the field you choose "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I look forward to starting my career with this company."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le07ob02aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "That's it. "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "You say this to mean there is no more of something or to finish a conversation. "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:<br> <span class=\"strong\">Susan</span>: Is there anything else I need to know?<br><span class=\"strong\">Michael</span>: No. That's it."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le07ob02aud07"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write an e-mail to a friend telling them that you got a new job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain why you accepted the job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain to your friends what you will miss from your old job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use first conditional sentences."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write an e-mail."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about jobs and work."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about future possibilities."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": 